From eb636ac6b9f0f285298a2fc90b3f60fd5f92c562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:55:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 346/638] protobuf: retain endian fallback helpers on AROS

Whole-archive CEF exposes a real Protobuf inclusion-order mismatch: wire_format.o retains the generic endian call path while coded_stream.o compiles as little endian. Emit the two correct out-of-line helpers on AROS so both object contracts are satisfied.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: archive nm attributes both unresolved helpers exclusively to protobuf_full/wire_format.o; compile commands otherwise differ only by the full-library feature set

AI_LIMITATIONS: focused object rebuild, native CEF link, and broader protobuf regression remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 third_party/protobuf/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/protobuf/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.cc b/third_party/protobuf/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.cc
index aacf007d7f..89dc54eaea 100644
--- a/third_party/protobuf/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.cc
+++ b/third_party/protobuf/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.cc
@@ -861,7 +861,11 @@ uint8_t* EpsCopyOutputStream::WriteAliasedRaw(const void* data, int size,
   }
 }
 
-#ifndef PROTOBUF_LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#if !defined(PROTOBUF_LITTLE_ENDIAN) || defined(__AROS__)
+// Whole-archive AROS consumers can combine generated objects whose header
+// inclusion order retains the generic endian path with this implementation
+// object compiled for little endian. Keep the two out-of-line helpers
+// available; their byte-order primitives remain correct on x86_64.
 uint8_t* EpsCopyOutputStream::WriteRawLittleEndian32(const void* data, int size,
                                                    uint8_t* ptr) {
   auto p = static_cast<const uint8_t*>(data);
